# Template for ai-service.env (a secret file, mode 600). install.sh creates
# ai-service.env from this file when it is missing, and asks for each API key
# whose line is empty. run.sh sources ai-service.env with bash, so keep to
# plain KEY=value lines and put single quotes around any value with spaces, $
# or parentheses (inside double quotes, bash still expands $).
# Restart the service after an edit.

# --- secrets ---
# Providers for /api/transcribe/stream: AssemblyAI Universal-3.5 Pro and/or
# Deepgram Nova-3. At least one is required, or the service refuses to start.
# With more than one, a tray picker appears and remembers the last choice in
# data/cache.db.
# AssemblyAI key. The mic stream goes to sync.assemblyai.com/v1/transcribe/live;
# ffmpeg decodes MediaRecorder WebM to PCM first.
ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=
# Deepgram key for Nova-3 live transcription. The mic stream goes to
# wss://api.deepgram.com/v1/listen; ffmpeg decodes MediaRecorder WebM to PCM
# first.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter key for MAI-Transcribe-2 on /api/transcribe-verbatim
# (daily-dictation). Separate from OPENROUTER_API_KEY below (that one is
# /api/explain's) so each route can keep its own key.
OPENROUTER_TRANSCRIBE_API_KEY=
# Key(s) for /api/explain: set one or both. With both, a tray picker chooses
# which provider answers; requests can never silently switch on their own.
# OpenRouter key for word explanations (not transcription).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Claude Platform key (api.anthropic.com).
CLAUDE_API_KEY=
# Key(s) for /api/ask: set one or more. The tray picker chooses which choice
# answers. A Claude or OpenRouter key creates two choices, with and without web
# search. These are separate from the explain and Memoir keys, so each route
# can use its own provider and credential.
# Claude Platform key (api.anthropic.com).
ASK_CLAUDE_API_KEY=
# Cerebras key (api.cerebras.ai).
ASK_CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter key for DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017. It exposes two choices: thinking
# effort high with OpenRouter's web search (Exa), and the same model with no
# search tool. Separate from OPENROUTER_API_KEY, which belongs to /api/explain.
ASK_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Key for /api/memoir/check: fill in EXACTLY ONE of the next two and leave the other
# empty. The service refuses to start with both set. Every Memoir variable
# starts with MEMOIR_, because the plain CLAUDE_API_KEY above is /api/explain's.
# Claude Platform key (api.anthropic.com).
MEMOIR_CLAUDE_API_KEY=
# Cerebras key. (Before 2026-10-20 this was called CEREBRAS_API_KEY; the old
# name makes the service refuse to start.)
MEMOIR_CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# --- transcription ---
# /api/transcribe/stream uses AssemblyAI's universal-3-5-pro and/or Deepgram's
# nova-3 live endpoint; ffmpeg decodes MediaRecorder WebM/MP4 to 16 kHz PCM.
# /api/transcribe-verbatim uses OpenRouter's microsoft/mai-transcribe-2 with
# verbose_json, word timestamps and Azure's verbatim style; OpenRouter caps
# those uploads at 25 MB. Model ids and endpoints are fixed in
# internal/server/assemblyai.go, internal/server/deepgram.go and
# internal/server/openrouter.go.

# --- models and thinking depth ---
# Models and thinking controls are fixed in internal/config, not environment
# settings: claude-opus-5-5 (effort medium) and
# deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 (reasoning effort high), each with a search
# and a no-search choice on /api/ask; google/gemini-3.8-flash (1024 thinking
# tokens for /api/explain); and qwen-3.8-27b (reasoning effort medium). Leftover
# *_EFFORT, *_REASONING_EFFORT and EXPLAIN_REASONING_TOKENS lines are ignored.
#
# /api/memoir/check model. Model id for the provider whose key is set above.
# Leave it unset for the default: claude-opus-5-5 on Claude, qwen-3.8-27b on
# Cerebras. With a Claude key the id must start with "claude-", or the service
# refuses to start.
#MEMOIR_MODEL=

# --- server ---
# The clients and install.sh's health check expect exactly this address.
LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8770

# --- paths: leave unset ---
# run.sh defaults it relative to this folder, so the folder can move without an
# edit. On Linux the service may only write data/ and logs/, so keep it inside
# data/.
# Default: <repo>/data/cache.db (the Merriam-Webster cache).
#CACHE_DB=
